WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.159
Avengers: Infinity War left a lot of dangling
questions.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.540
Among the most important: where was the Hulk?

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.500
The big green guy all but abandoned Bruce
Banner in the battle against Thanos.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.200
Was his absence just build-up for an Endgame
triumph?

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.400
It's a good bet that he'll be back in the
big Infinity Saga finale, which makes us ask

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.800
one big question: could a vengeful Hulk actually
put Thanos to bed permanently?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.960
Here's all the ways we think that might happen.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.739
One of the most defining elements of the Hulk
is that the mean green brute is strong.

00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:29.439
Really, really strong.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:33.710
There are so many layers of pure, unadulterated
muscle that it has always been a primary trait

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:38.989
over the decades, whether it be on the printed
page, television set, or cinematic universe.

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:42.260
After all, the Hulk's the best there is at
what he does, and what he does is, well…

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.780
“Hulk Smash!"

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.960
At this point, everyone knows that if you
hit Hulk hard, you're only going to be hit

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:53.660
back harder.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.160
Of course, this natural ability to "muscle
up" makes Hulk a prime choice to use in any

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.500
kind of one-on-one showdown.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.240
If Hulk starts smashing, you can bet there's
a fair chance that Thanos' demise might occur

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.210
under those two giant green fists.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.100
But, of course, the question that naturally
arises from that statement is whether he'll

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.760
start smashing in the first place.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.340
The biggest mystery about the Hulk when it
comes to Infinity War is just where he was

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.680
during the whole ordeal.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.900
When push came to shove, with the universe
at stake, Hulk was a non-starter.

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:25.939
He had a peek around, took a few lumps from
Thanos, and called it quits quicker than anyone

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:26.840
else in the film.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.900
Of course, that doesn't mean Hulk was really
done.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.820
Anyone who watches that opening scene can
pretty quickly see that the Jade Giant wasn't

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:33.950
quite in character.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.240
He looks dazed, confused, and half-committed.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.300
It turns out, according to the Russos themselves,
Hulk wasn't so much scared by the confrontation

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.080
as genuinely angry about it.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.640
Director Joe Russo stated plainly on the commentary
track:

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.560
"People have speculated on whether there was
some fear on the Hulk's part about having

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:55.649
to face Thanos again but I think ultimately,
what it is, is that he's tired of playing

00:01:55.649 --> 00:01:57.799
hero to Bruce Banner."

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:01.070
And after two years spent in control on Sakaar,
can you blame him?

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.390
Regardless, if Hulk's going to stop Thanos,
he's going to need to get over his hurt feelings

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.940
and take the reins once again.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.660
Of course, Hulk's absence actually plays nicely
into his chances of dealing the final blow

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.840
to the Mad Titan.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.540
As of the end of Infinity War, Thanos sees
the Hulk as nothing more than a passing annoyance.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.760
His attention in Endgame will probably be
more focused on characters like Thor, who

00:02:20.761 --> 00:02:24.629
already stabbed him in the chest, and Captain
Marvel, who's been confirmed to be the most

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:26.940
powerful superhero in the MCU.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.120
This could play into the Avengers' hands nicely,
as everyone else knows that Hulk really is

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.820
one of their best chances at beating the living
daylights out of Thanos.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.590
Perhaps, rather than a straight-up brawl,
it'll be the element of surprise that could

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.560
help the Hulk rise to the occasion and be
the one to take down Thanos.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.280
Once Hulk gets over his hurt feelings, he
might feel a twinge of embarrassment at having

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.800
left everyone to fend for themselves during
what was clearly the largest crisis that the

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:52.680
Avengers have ever faced.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:57.060
If he really did sit out because he was being
a baby about the whole losing control issue,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:01.030
once he has a chance to process things with
Banner, he might even feel a little remorse

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.060
and regret at how everything went down.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.900
Plus, the fact that he was made to look like
a fool could give Hulk a healthy dose of inspiration,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.460
not to mention a vendetta against the guy
who made him look like an idiot while he was

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:12.400
taking a time-out.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.460
Before we move on to more specific ways that
Hulk could take down Thanos, let's talk about

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.440
one more "big picture" element that could
factor in here.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:21.800
Hulk is strong, sure.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.620
But, honestly, he's not the only member on
the team that can go toe-to-toe with Thanos

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.720
and have a fighting chance.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.140
Even Iron Man got him to bleed a little, right?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.420
"All that for a drop of blood."

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.920
But one thing the Hulk has that the others
don't is the exponential scaling of his rage.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:37.939
Hulk literally thrives in adversity.

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:41.650
If he feels outmatched, he gets angry and
his strength scales along with it.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.600
He's virtually untouched by fear, too.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.709
If the Green Goliath can get angry early enough
in a fight with Thanos, there's a good chance

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:51.080
the Mad Titan side of that equation is going
to have a rough go of it.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.160
While the thought of a furious Hulk giving
Thanos a run for his money is as good as gold,

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.900
there's one weapon that Hulk could use that
would make the entire affair that much better.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:04.540
For a while now it's been heavily rumored
that Tony Stark's part in the endgame of Endgame

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.600
involves him reassembling the Avengers and
building his own Infinity Gauntlet.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.739
Another rumor indicated that it might be none
other than the Hulk who wields the second

00:04:12.739 --> 00:04:14.829
gauntlet in battle against Thanos.

00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:18.880
The theory even comes with the added speculation
that Hulk may end up losing an arm in the

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.380
process.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.400
Whether he loses an arm or not, though, the
simple fact that Hulk could end up wielding

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.020
the Infinity Stones could give him all the
power he needs to kill Thanos.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.720
While it's fun to think up "Hulk smash" scenarios
that could lead to Thanos' demise, the truth

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:35.600
is that after Infinity War, there seems to
be something of a Hulk special being cooked

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.180
up at Marvel Studios.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.500
A while back, actor Mark Ruffalo explained
that the Hulk had a story arc taking place

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:46.530
over the course of three separate movies:
Thor: Ragnarok, Avengers: Infinity War, and

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.260
Avengers: Endgame.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.480
This led to a bunch of rumors that point to
the idea that Hulk's story may actually end

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.450
in reconciliation between himself and Bruce
Banner.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:58.550
A burying of the hatchet between the two could
finally pave the way for the arrival of Professor

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.740
Hulk, a version of the character who has the
brains of Banner and the brawn of the Hulk.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.360
A Hulk that's as smart as he is strong could
be just hero to finally take down Thanos.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.340
Speaking of Professor Hulk, even if we're
fairly certain about his appearance in Endgame,

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.300
Marvel Studios has been tight-lipped about
how the synthesized character could actually

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:16.800
appear.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.740
And, of course, whenever Marvel is reticent
about something, the fans are ready to step

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:21.660
up to the plate.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:26.120
One particularly interesting theory about
the transformation actually involves The Ancient

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.760
One, Tilda Swinton's character in Doctor Strange.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.430
The theory suggests that Banner will head
back in time along with everyone else via

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.520
the Quantum Realm.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.460
Once there, he'll cross paths with the Ancient
One, who will help teach him how to control

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.780
his anger and bring about the healing that
the two so desperately need.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:45.200
There's some evidence to support it, too:
Mark Ruffalo did refer to working with Swinton

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.620
in an unnamed project back in 2017.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:51.900
The Ancient One has also been reported to
be among the action figures being made for

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.200
Endgame, so it's certainly possible.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.980
While there's no doubt that Hulk is a top
contender to take Thanos down, he's certainly

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.680
not the only option on the table.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.240
In fact, there are quite a few other people
who are actively standing in line in front

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:03.740
of him.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:07.760
The guilt-laden Tony Stark has a laundry list
of reasons to be the guy who takes the kill

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.260
shot.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:12.940
Nebula's list might be even longer at this
point, and besides, she was critical in toppling

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.000
Thanos in the Infinity Gauntlet comics.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.140
Thor is just plain angry about everything
at this point and wants some revenge somewhere.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:23.710
But even if someone else actually kills Thanos,
Hulk could be an instrumental piece of that

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.400
scenario simply by being a distraction.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.400
How often do the Avengers get the important
stuff done while Hulk is busy doing the dirty

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:29.900
work?

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:34.340
In the Battle of New York, Cap led the team
and Iron Man saved everyone's butts by dealing

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.060
with the nuke.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:39.220
But Hulk was the point man, taking down alien
hordes right and left in a spectacle that

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.460
drew a ton of attention.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:41.460
"And Hulk.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:44.940
Smash!"

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.020
He's done the same in numerous other battles.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.060
If his ultimate role is to play the distractor,
he'd know the part backward and forward by

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:56.560
now.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.140
Another way that Hulk could ultimately kill
Thanos might be by simply stepping aside and

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.070
letting Bruce Banner do the work for him.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:07.220
While he may have been dodging his responsibilities
in Infinity War, getting the Hulk to come

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:10.360
out and play isn't necessarily the key to
everything going well.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.520
In fact, puny Bruce Banner may have a much
more important part to play than we think.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:18.960
One heavily rumored element that could be
critical in Endgame is the aforementioned

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.700
time travel via the Quantum Realm.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:24.700
The problem is, who's going to be able help
everyone move back and forth through time?

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:28.460
Scott Lang has the experience, but he's lacking
the scientific know-how.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:32.280
Shuri might be able to do it, but based on
what we've seen in the Endgame trailer, she's

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.100
fallen victim to Thanos' snap.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.840
At the end of the day, having someone like
Bruce Banner on hand to guide the team through

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.870
the Quantum Realm could be just the brainy
ticket the team needs to take Thanos down.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:46.160
We've spent a good amount of time breaking
down Hulk's furious rage and how it could

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.280
be a factor, but one popular theory is that
we'll get to see World Breaker Hulk.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.820
Who is World Breaker Hulk?

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.720
In essence, it's the strongest manifestation
of Hulk that we've ever gotten to see in the

00:07:55.730 --> 00:08:00.240
comic books, and certainly one that could
give Thanos a run for his money, with or without

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.120
his fancy pants Infinity Gauntlet.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.940
One popular fan theory pointed out that the
timing would be pretty fitting.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.061
Thor has pretty much finished his evolution
into a nearly all-powerful being, while Hulk

00:08:10.061 --> 00:08:12.580
is lagging behind and due for a story arc
finale.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.980
And, as we know, Avengers: Endgame represents
the end of the arc that Mark Ruffalo has discussed

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.520
in interviews in the past.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.670
Perhaps the stars are aligning for World Breaker
Hulk to take on Thanos and reverse the results

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:23.660
of their first meeting.

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.740
Whether it's due to his strength, his fury,
a second Infinity Gauntlet, or anything else,

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.340
Hulk needs to have one more critical factor
going in his favor if he's going to topple

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.590
the Mad Titan: he needs to have an interest.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:38.960
Hulk's care-free attitude toward Thanos has
crippled his ability to have any positive

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.400
impact on the storyline.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.300
On the contrary, his actions seem to have
simply allowed the universe to go to hell

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.300
in a handbasket.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.460
No matter how many Captain Marvels or Ant-Men
show up to try and save the day in Endgame,

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.690
Hulk is going to need to get his act together
in the big Avengers finale.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:57.310
He has to get over any petty squabbles with
Banner and team up to focus on the true danger

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:57.860
at hand.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.600
Both characters have serious upsides, especially
if they're working together.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.260
Oh, and Banner's probably going to need to
get angry.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.100
"I'm always angry."

